{"name":"Paying Mantis","hex":"#70916c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paying","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of pay"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["payment"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paying"},{"term":"mantis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various large insects of the order Mantodea that catch insects or other small animals with their powerful forelegs.","A green colour, like that of many mantises. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mantis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Payment","blocks":[{"text":"A payment is the tender of something of value, such as money or its equivalent, by one party to another in exchange for goods or services provided by them, or to fulfill a legal obligation or philanthropy desire. The party making the payment is commonly called the payer, while the payee is the party receiving the payment. Whilst payments are often made voluntarily, some payments are compulsory, such as payment of a fine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/TaiwanMoney_card_in_use_in_Hi-Life_20051223.jpg/330px-TaiwanMoney_card_in_use_in_Hi-Life_20051223.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Payment"},{"title":"Mantis","blocks":[{"text":"Mantises are an order (Mantodea) of insects that contains over 2,400 species in about 460 genera in 33 families. The largest family is the Mantidae (\"mantids\"). Mantises are distributed worldwide in temperate and tropical habitats. They have triangular heads with bulging eyes supported on flexible necks. Their elongated bodies may or may not have wings, but all mantodeans have forelegs that are greatly enlarged and adapted for catching and gripping prey; their upright posture, while remaining stationary with forearms folded, resembling a praying posture, has led to the common name praying mantis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Mantis_%28European%29.jpg/330px-Mantis_%28European%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantis"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg/500px-2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg/1280px-2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg/500px-2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stagmomantis carolina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2021-09-17_Stagmomantis_carolina.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Santanmantis_reconstruction.png/500px-Santanmantis_reconstruction.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Santanmantis_reconstruction.png/1280px-Santanmantis_reconstruction.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.